; ============================================================================
; 68k ROM: header and code (FFC00000)
; ============================================================================
; ROM offset 000000-0D34FF = physical FFC00000-FFCD34FF; the 68k ROM is used in place
; (ROMBase = $FFC00000 in low memory after boot), interpreted by the 68k emulator.
; Header: checksum 960E4BE9, reset PC +2A, machine 07 version 7D, release 34F2,
; resources at +D4D00, trap dispatch tables at +D3500, 68k ROM size 300000.
; Disassembled as 68040 code by MAME's 68k disassembler. Entry points: the header
; vectors, every trap implementation in the dispatch tables (labels _TrapName), and the
; 68k instructions executed in the coverage run (the emulator's PC, r24, at dispatch).
; A-line traps are shown by name; low-memory globals by name in the comments.
;
; Columns: address, flag, raw bytes, instruction, ; comment.
;   flag '*' executed in the coverage run, ' ' reached by control flow,
;   '?' decodes as code but neither executed nor reached, 'd' data.

